# Writer boundary of the atom counter. Format: path|function|families|reason
# families: T tip (mk:) · C conflict/history rows · B atom body · N atom counter · M molecule header counters · R blob counter and blob queue · - none of these
# One line for each function that the lint finds. The lint fails on a function that is missing,
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/atom_history/policy.rs|set_field_history_policy|C|writes only a canonical field policy and the logical format fence in one native transaction; no tip, archive, atom, or reference counter write
# on a function that names a family the line does not list, and on a line that no function matches.
# `*` as the function is for the planner module only.

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/metadata_store/idempotency.rs|retire_legacy|-|bounded cleanup inside the reserved idempotency namespace; deletes only validated legacy idem keys and writes its cleanup marker in the native request snapshot; no tip, atom or counter keys

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/delete_replay.rs|raise_replay_cutoff|-|explicit stopped-home maintenance (`lastdb db recount --delete-cutoff`): puts the one replay cutoff row; no record, history, blob counter or conflict row


fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/counter/commit.rs|*|C|the row commit: releases rcf: conflict rows, writes queue and blob planner rows and guarded deletes in one batch_mutate that joins the pending batch of the request
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/blob_counter/commit.rs|*|R|the blob planner: blob counters and queue entries change in the batch of the record write (records.rs), or in the request scope of a blob row put
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/blob_counter/dwell_chunk.rs|*|R|the dwell chunk: reads the counter again in the write gate, then deletes the blob row, the counter and the queue entry in one batch (the retirement of a bucket is the guarded delete of the planner)
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/blob_counter/recount.rs|*|R|the blob step of the offline recount: writes the exact blob counters and deletes stale queue entries on a stopped home, in whole batches


fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/admin_db/history_prune.rs|clear_mutation_history|C|clear-history deletes history rows that are not conflict rows (a conflict row keeps its atom references)







fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/keep_small.rs|clear_keep_small_distrust_marker|-|keep-small meter distrust marker
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/keep_small.rs|note_keep_small_hydrate_failure|-|keep-small meter distrust marker




fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/conflict_index_heal.rs|prune_conflict_index|C|rewrites the mcc: id list inside a write scope; the list holds no atom reference
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/conflict_index_heal.rs|stamp_conflict_index|C|rewrites the mcc: id list inside a write scope; the list holds no atom reference

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/conflict_operations/home_index.rs|delete_event_keys|C|hcu: home conflict events and stamp; they hold no atom reference
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/conflict_operations/home_index.rs|write_home_conflict_stamp|C|hcu: home conflict events and stamp; they hold no atom reference


# db_catalog_store.rs::drop_scoped_source_rows deletes every row of one scope through a store argument (tips, bodies and counters go together). The lint cannot see keys that a caller hands to it.




fold_db/crates/core/src/storage/encrypting_store/kv_store_impl.rs|restore_batch_put|T C B N|store layer: passes a restored row to the inner store


fold_db/crates/core/src/storage/traits/kv.rs|restore_batch_put|T C B N|store trait: default restore of one row


































lastdb_node/src/bin/received_range_seed.rs|activate_generated_receivers|-|CI-only generated share_subscriptions controls in an isolated owned home; mutation manager owns all tip, atom, and counter writes
lastdb_node/src/bin/received_range_seed.rs|activate_generated_send_rule|-|CI-only generated share_rules control for the send check in an isolated owned home; mutation manager owns all tip, atom, record, and counter writes




fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/erase_meters.rs|record_atom_delete_audit|-|final dellog audit facts only, optionally database-prefixed; staged in the same native batch as the erase, with no atom, tip, or counter keys
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/counter/restore_validation.rs|finish|-|exclusive restore completion deletes only its durable pending marker after exact read-only counter verification

fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/records.rs|stage_records|-|format 7 home: puts rk: record values, their ak: entry changes, the rh: field history copies with their ahq: queue and ahk: count rows, and the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations in one native batch; creates no atom, field tip, archive row or atom counter
fold_db/crates/core/src/db_operations/atom_store/atom_history/records.rs|commit_history_release|-|format 7 home: releases rh: field history copies with their ahq: queue entries, ahk: count rows and the blob planner rows of blob_counter_mutations in one native batch; no tip, atom, archive row or atom counter
# Conversion coverage lives in its own namespace, never the atom store.
